==Strategy==
This is one of the first stages to emphasise the importance of [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Control]]. Red Cyclone's massive damage per hit and DPS do not allow for resistant units to do much at all. For this reason, even the toughest tank turns into a waste of money immediately, so it should be avoided. Instead, this stage should be beaten with anti-Red/Floating Crowd-Controllers to halt its advance reliably. Cats that work well are [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]] (whose True Form makes this stage trivial), [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]], [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]] or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], as well as some [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] and collab cats that affect [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and/or [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] (like [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]]). Cats with extra damage can be helpful to quickly kill the enemies, so they should also be used if available.


